{"id":"W7a973799256a316d3c5e8175","zh":"","en":"KLE","name":"KLE","language":"en","domain":"随机场方法","concept_id":"Ce20a3a2a2c51d085b1e8","families":[{"id":"stochastic.spectral","label":"随机过程与谱分析"}],"definition_zh":"利用特征值、特征函数或特征向量与随机系数表示随机过程或随机场的展开。","definition_en":null,"scope_note":null,"usage_note":null,"usage_overview":"通过协方差核或协方差、相关矩阵的特征分解，将随机过程或随机场表示为确定性模态与随机系数的组合，并以有限项截断实现离散和降维；用于轨道不平顺、参数空间变异及风速过程的随机模拟与动力分析。","translation_note":null,"usage_variants":[],"designations":[{"id":"W7a973799256a316d3c5e8175","text":"KLE","language":"en","role":"headword"}],"complete_examples":[{"id":"Sd84eab6bea7d02f8b56b","source_id":"P010","page":12,"page_end":12,"language":"en","text":"In the current work, Karhunen–Loève Expansion (KLE) is further applied to achieve a dimensional reduction for the random filed of track-bridge systems.","citations":[{"source_id":"P010","page":12,"page_end":12}]},{"id":"Se3b66cf3d906d04046a1","source_id":"P010","page":17,"page_end":17,"language":"en","text":"As observed from Fig. 10 , the results of these two methods are in agreement with each other well, but the MCM-KLE approach greatly reduces the time-consuming of computation.","citations":[{"source_id":"P010","page":17,"page_end":17}]},{"id":"S60dae71efd2aa479001f","source_id":"P011","page":14,"page_end":14,"language":"en","text":"The details about KLE can be consulted in Refs. [27,28].","citations":[{"source_id":"P011","page":14,"page_end":14}]},{"id":"S9b34af999f7380ef1c34","source_id":"P052","page":10,"page_end":10,"language":"en","text":"The realization of multi-dimensional random fields based on KLE and the iteration algorithm of random samples is shown in Fig. 3.","citations":[{"source_id":"P052","page":10,"page_end":10}]},{"id":"Sdcc1ddac52971f2412b8","source_id":"P052","page":23,"page_end":23,"language":"en","text":"A general numerical scheme in combination of KLE is introduced to realize the multi-dimensional random field of the track system, which is specified by arbitrarily probability distribution and covariance function.","citations":[{"source_id":"P052","page":23,"page_end":23}]},{"id":"S879da451d905936903e2","source_id":"P057","page":12,"page_end":12,"language":"en","text":"Applying the criterion and analysis demonstrated above, 100 track irregularity samples are adopted by KLE and TIPM methods.","citations":[{"source_id":"P057","page":12,"page_end":12}]},{"id":"S3b21ff6556486f7fbe12","source_id":"P057","page":14,"page_end":14,"language":"en","text":"However, the completeness of data information for the KLE method has a significant impact on the frequency domain characteristics.","citations":[{"source_id":"P057","page":14,"page_end":14}]}],"sources":{"P010":{"id":"P010","title":"A coupled model for train-track-bridge stochastic analysis with consideration of spatial variation and temporal evolution","authors":"L Xu, W Zhai, Z Li","year":"2018","doi":"10.1016/j.apm.2018.07.001","journal_citation":"Applied Mathematical Modelling 63, 709-731","label":"Xu等（2018）","overview_slug":"2018-a-coupled-model-for-train-track-bridge-stochastic-analysis-with-consideration-of-spatial-variation-a"},"P011":{"id":"P011","title":"A model for vehicle–track random interactions on effects of crosswinds and track irregularities","authors":"L Xu, W Zhai","year":"2019","doi":"10.1080/00423114.2018.1469775","journal_citation":"Vehicle system dynamics 57 (3), 444-469","label":"Xu等（2019）","overview_slug":"2019-a-model-for-vehicle-track-random-interactions-on-effects-of-crosswinds-and-track-irregularities"},"P052":{"id":"P052","title":"Development of a model for stochastic analysis of vehicle–track interaction considering spatial variability of track parameters","authors":"H Liu, L Xu","year":"2023","doi":"10.1016/j.probengmech.2022.103383","journal_citation":"Probabilistic Engineering Mechanics 72, 103383","label":"Liu等（2023）","overview_slug":"2023-development-of-a-model-for-stochastic-analysis-of-vehicle-track-interaction-considering-spatial-vari"},"P057":{"id":"P057",